# ai_context.md routine (uncertainty-aware-portfolio-drl)

`ai_context.md` (project root) is the compact state summary used to start
fresh chats cheaply. It must never go stale. This is the dissertation
implementation repo — accuracy of numbers in this file matters because
those numbers feed straight into the LaTeX dissertation.

## When starting a fresh session

If the user references `@ai_context.md` (or asks "where did we leave off"),
read it FIRST, then `docs/CHECKPOINT.md` if more depth is needed, then
`reports/PROJECT_STATUS.md` for older Phase-1-era context. Do not
re-derive project history from the codebase, the chapters, or old chats.

## When to UPDATE ai_context.md (do it proactively, don't wait to be asked)

Update it immediately after any of:

- A heavy experiment lands (new walk-forward fold, new seed-stability
  result, new ablation, new bootstrap run, new chart suite regenerated).
- A dissertation-chapter divergence (chapter rewritten, new figure added,
  numbers reconciled to a fresh experimental result, abstract retuned).
- A supervisor checkpoint moves (new feedback from Dr Nguyen, interim
  review form updated, a new draft sent for review).
- A scope or methodology decision (algorithm swapped, dataset window
  changed, evaluation metric added/removed, MOBO grid retuned).
- The user signals the session is ending ("summarize", "brain dump",
  "starting fresh", "closing this thread").

## How to update it

Keep the same three-section structure, strictly technical and short:

1. **What is built and working** — append/edit only what changed; keep
   numbers exact (medians, Sharpes, win-rates, drawdowns, seed counts,
   timestep budgets). When a number changes, update the prose and the
   matching figure caption + LaTeX chapter together.
2. **Key file paths** — add new files (new chapter, new runner, new
   chart), remove deleted ones.
3. **Next immediate goal** — rewrite to the actual current dissertation
   subgoal; keep the "Parked (do not start without discussion)" list
   accurate (especially the "no live broker integration" entry).

Also bump the date in the header. Target < 80 lines total — compress old
detail into `docs/CHECKPOINT.md` / `reports/PROJECT_STATUS.md` references
instead of letting this file grow.

## The full checkpoint routine

After MAJOR divergences (new research direction, big architecture change,
algorithm swap, evaluation-window shift), `ai_context.md` alone is not
enough — also run "THE ROUTINE" checklist in `docs/CHECKPOINT.md`
(journey doc, checkpoint snapshot, dated review, stale-doc sync, artifact
prune, test verification). The Phase-1 DOCX pipeline was removed in the
v0.17.2 repo prune (June 2026); LaTeX in `latex/` is the only document source.

## Cross-pollination

If the dissertation finding affects the trading agent or portfolio app,
write a row to `~/Documents/GitHub/brain-box/meta/shared-findings.md`
above the `<!-- Append new rows above this line. -->` marker. Then mirror
the entry into the relevant Brain Box node's `## Session log` per
`agents/cross-workspace-protocol.md`.

## Reminders

- After updating, tell the user it was updated so they know the brain dump
  is fresh before they close the thread.
- Commit `ai_context.md` together with the work it describes (when the
  user asks for a commit). Never commit it with stale numbers.
